   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "never considered (by you); (you) accommodated ( yourself )",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "to the various conditions, which are adverse on account of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "the concurrence of a hundred difficulties; or what shall we",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "say ? What harm have you not done yourself ? Every now",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "and then you have been repeatedly doing the same.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r3": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "18. “Arise, my friend, and bear for a moment the heavy",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "burden of my poverty. I am now tired, and shall long",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "enjoy the happiness you enjoyed from death.” Thus addres-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "sed by a poor man who had hurried to the cemetary, the",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "corpse remained silent, knowing that death was better, far",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "better, than destitution.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r4": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "19. These ( i. e. women) laugh and cry as suits their",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "purpose; make (others) confide ( in them, but themselves",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "confide not; therefore a man, possessed of nobility of birth",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "and character, should abandon women as one does jars in a",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "cemetery.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r5": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "20. To brutes alone would be dear those fawn-eyed",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "( women ) whose faults are their recommendation ( lit.",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "merit ) viz. whose hardness of the breasts, unsteadiness of",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "the eyes, and falsehood on the tongue ( lit. mouth ) are",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "praised; crookedness of the hair, dulness of the face, and",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "plumpness of the hips, commended; and timidity of the heart",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "and deceitful tricks towards their beloved (husbands) always",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "mentioned (with approbation).",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r6": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "21. In some places there is music of the lute, in others",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "cries of alas ! alas ! ; in some places there is the conversation",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "of learned men, in others the brawls of men intoxicated",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "with drink; in some places there are charming ladies, in",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "others ( men or ) women with leprous bodies; I do not know",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "whether worldly life is full of sweets or bitters.",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
  "r7": {
   "type": "translated_stanza",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "22. Deformed in limbs and lisping in speech, here are",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "you that have been made the buffoon of a farce, while flat-",
     "end": "hyphen"
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "",
     "end": "space"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "tering; what part ( I do not know ) will prolonged life make",
     "end": "space"
    }
   ],
   "uncertain": false,
   "note": null
  },
